# Mood Match - environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in as needed. `.env` is gitignored and is NEVER
# uploaded with the scene (the leading dot is covered by `.dclignore`).
#
#   cp .env.example .env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Private key of the wallet that owns the Decentraland NAME you are deploying to.
# Only needed for NON-INTERACTIVE deploys (CI, or ./deploy.sh without a browser).
# Leave this unset for local deploys and sign in the browser instead - that is
# safer, because the key never has to exist on disk.
#
# In GitHub Actions, set this as a repository SECRET named DCL_PRIVATE_KEY,
# never as a plain variable and never committed here.
DCL_PRIVATE_KEY=

# The World this scene deploys to, e.g. mood-match.dcl.eth
# This is read by ./deploy.sh only as a convenience; the value that actually
# ships is `worldConfiguration.name` in scene.json.
DCL_WORLD_NAME=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side runtime values (Multiplayer Server)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Values the headless server reads with `EnvVar.get()` are NOT taken from this
# file in production. Set those on the live scene instead, where they stay
# server-side and never reach the client:
#
#   npx sdk-commands storage env set KEY --value VALUE
#
# or through the Environment tab at https://decentraland.org/storage
#
# Mood Match currently reads no environment variables at runtime - all tuning
# lives in src/shared/config.ts so that the client and server can never
# disagree about the rules. This section is here for when that changes.
